    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just a \"temporary state\" though. i see the way they look at me. they're so proud of what they thought i'd become, and now i'm just this disappointment. it's like, if i hadn't happened, if i hadn't messed up, they could just keep that pride intact. instead, i'm just the part of the story where everything went wrong. it feels like i'm just dragging them down with me every single day.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The pressure you feel to live up to their dreams is crushing, but you are far more than their expectations. Your worth isn't tied to a perfect outcome; it's in the fact that you are here, even when things feel broken. Instead of viewing yourself as a failure, see yourself as someone who is hurting and needs a way to find the right path forward.",
      "source": "target",
